  "english": "14. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Father [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"O Lord, God of our fathers\" (Astuats harts'n merots).\n\n18. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 5 [g3]: \"Glorified Son\" (P’araworeal vordi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Christ rose\" (K’ristos yareaw), and \"Morning\" (Arawotean), and \"They anticipated\" (Kankhets’in).\n\n24. Saturday. Tone 2 [AK]. Of David the Prophet, and of James the Apostle.\n\n25. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhayawitean). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [b3]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zouarchats’an).\n\n29. Thursday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Of the Sons of Thunder: James and John. Fast-Break [Barekendan] of the Nativity Fast.\n\nJanuary:\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Sixth [Sunday] of the Fast. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: \"Wondrous Resurrection\" (Hrashali zyarent’iun).\n\n2. Monday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Of the Fast. Father [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed Lord God, blessed\" (Orhneal ter astuats orhneal).\n\n5. Thursday. Tone 6 [GK]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ [Chragaloyts].\n\n28. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Of Julian and Basilissa. Father [Harts] Tone 7 [dz]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord\" (Surb es ter).\n\nAnd see the others in the First Volume until the end, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember:\n\n4. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Who art the King\" (Or t’agaword es). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk]: \"To reveal and our\" (Arhral ew mer).\n\n5. Monday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Of Gennarius, and Mercurius; and of James and Iratp’ar [Haratp’ar].\n\n6. Tuesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Of Abgar the King. Read the Lection and Gospel of Theodosius.\n\n9. Friday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n11. Sunday. Tone 5 [GDZ]. Third [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who in the form of a servant\" (Or tsarayi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [g3]: \"Glorified is Thy\" (P’araworeal e k’o). Fast-Break [Barekendan] of the Fast of Saint James.\n\nO\n\nTHE SEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 5.\n\nJanuary:\n\n6. WEDNESDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period of eating [non-fasting days] is nineteen days.\n\n14. Thursday. Of John the Forerunner.\n\n16. Saturday. Of Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n\n17. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 7 [dz]: \"Dawn of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n\n18. Monday. Of Anton, and Triphon, Barsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n\n19. Tuesday. Of Theodosius the King, and the Holy Babes of Ephesus.\n\n21. Thursday. Of Cyriacus and Julitta.\n\n23. Saturday. Of Athanasius and Cyril the Patriarchs.\n\n24. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Fast-Break [Barekendan] of the Catechumens [Arachavorats]. And see the others until the Fourth [Sunday] of Vardavar in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary:\n\n14. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Great Fast-Break [Bun Barekendan]. — Presentation of the Lord [Tearnndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nApril:\n\n4. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection of Christ.\n\n7. Wednesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary. See according to the order in the First Volume.",
